<LegalLayout title="Grievance redressal" eyebrow="Legal / 05" currentPage="/grievance-redressal" intro="How to raise a service, privacy, booking or website concern with Crest Automotive Care and request an internal review.">
  <h2>1. First contact</h2>
  <p><strong>Crest Automotive Solutions LLP, trading as Crest Automotive Care</strong>, receives service, privacy, booking and website grievances at <a href="mailto:ruchirm01@gmail.com">ruchirm01@gmail.com</a>. You may also call <a href="tel:+919871610952">+91 98716 10952</a> or use the enquiry form on the <a href="/#contact">main website</a>.</p>
  <p>Please include your name, phone number, vehicle, booking or invoice reference, date of service, the issue, and the outcome you are seeking. Do not send payment-card passwords, one-time passwords or unnecessary sensitive information.</p>

  <h2>2. Internal review process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>We will acknowledge the complaint after receiving and reviewing the basic details.</li>
    <li>We will review the booking, communications, invoice, vehicle condition and relevant service records.</li>
    <li>We may request photographs, an inspection appointment or additional information.</li>
    <li>We will communicate a proposed resolution or reasoned response after the review, subject to complexity and third-party dependencies.</li>
    <li>If the matter remains unresolved, reply to the same email thread so the matter can be escalated within Crest Automotive Solutions LLP.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>3. Privacy grievances</h2>
  <p>For a request about personal data, consent, correction, deletion, access or a suspected privacy incident, write to <a href="mailto:ruchirm01@gmail.com">ruchirm01@gmail.com</a> and mark the subject “Privacy grievance”. We may verify your identity before responding. See the <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for more detail.</p>

  <h2>4. Consumer assistance</h2>
  <p>The Government of India’s Department of Consumer Affairs describes a three-tier Consumer Commission system and provides access to consumer-grievance resources. If an internal resolution does not address your concern, you may review official information through the <a href="https://consumeraffairs.gov.in/pages/consumer-protection-unit" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Department of Consumer Affairs</a> and the <a href="https://consumerhelpline.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Consumer Helpline</a>.</p>
  <p>Official consumer-help channels and contact numbers may change. Use the current details published on the official government websites rather than relying on a copied number in this policy.</p>

  <h2>5. No retaliation</h2>
  <p>We will not penalise a customer for raising a genuine complaint or exercising an applicable legal right. We may limit communications where a message is abusive, threatening, fraudulent or unrelated to a genuine service or privacy issue.</p>

  <h2>6. Policy owner and contact</h2>
  <p>Policy owner: <strong>Crest Automotive Solutions LLP, trading as Crest Automotive Care</strong>. Grievance contact: <a href="mailto:ruchirm01@gmail.com">ruchirm01@gmail.com</a>. Telephone: <a href="tel:+919871610952">+91 98716 10952</a>. Effective date: <strong>22 August 2026</strong>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
